IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-super`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- superannuation amounts the text deposit could not compute,
-- now computed from the formulas the Federal Register prints as images: the indexation of the superannuation caps and
-- thresholds (s 960-285(2) to (7), the factor in s 960-285(5)); the concessional contributions cap (s 291-20(2)), the general
-- transfer balance cap (s 294-35(3)) and the large and very large superannuation balance thresholds (ss 296-30, 296-35) for
-- any year; the non-concessional cap built from them (s 292-85(2)); proportional indexation of your own transfer balance cap
-- (s 294-40(2)); your defined benefit income cap (s 303-4(1)); and your Division 296 taxable superannuation earnings and very
-- large superannuation balance earnings component (ss 296-40, 296-45).
--
-- A module beside itaa-super.l4 (24 October 2026). itaa-super.l4 takes the indexed caps as supplied numbers ("passed in") and
-- left s 294-40 out; it stays as it is. This module works those numbers out and calls itaa-super.l4's rules
-- (`What is my non-concessional cap`, `What is my excess transfer balance`) rather than restating them.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who contributes to super or draws a pension from it ("What is my cap this year?", "Is any of my
-- super's earnings taxed under Division 296?").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267 (register id C2026C00400), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The
-- formulas are images the text deposit dropped; they are transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md
-- (entries s 960-285(5), s 294-40(2), s 303-4(1), s 296-40(1)(b), (2), s 296-45(1), (2); recovered 2026-10-24), and encoded
-- from there.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ARE NOT LAW. s 960-285(7): the index number is the AWOTE estimate of s 960-280(4) (the concessional cap) or the
-- All Groups CPI of s 960-280(1) (the transfer balance cap and the Division 296 thresholds). Those are figures the Australian
-- Statistician publishes; none is deposited, so each is an input. Your total superannuation earnings (s 296-55) are worked
-- out from what your funds report (s 296-60) and are an input here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Subdivision 294-E (child recipients); s 303-4(2) and (3) (a part year, and defined benefit income outside
-- ss 301-10, 301-100, 302-65, 302-85); s 296-50 (death), ss 296-20 and 296-25 (exceptions, asked as one fact), ss 296-55 to
-- 296-75 (how total superannuation earnings are worked out); the amount of Division 296 tax (the Superannuation (Building a
-- Stronger and Fairer Super System) Imposition Act 2026, not deposited); a change of CPI reference period (s 960-280(3)).
-- Years are named by the calendar year in which they begin: 2025 is the 2025-26 financial year.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- superannuation amounts from the formulas`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger amount of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller amount of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `960-285 -- indexing the superannuation caps`

-- s 960-285(5), from the authorised rendering (C2004A05138.formulas.md):
--     *Index number mentioned in subsection (7) for the *quarter ending on 31 December just before the start of the relevant
--     income year or *financial year / *Index number mentioned in subsection (7) for the base quarter
-- (6): "You work out the *indexation factor mentioned in subsection (5) to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal
-- place is 5 or more)."
@export What is the indexation factor for a superannuation cap or threshold (s 960-285(5), (6))?
GIVEN `index number for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The index number for the quarter ending on 31 December just before the start of the year (AWOTE for the concessional cap, the All Groups CPI for the transfer balance cap and the Division 296 thresholds)
      `index number for the base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The same index number for the base quarter (the quarter ending 31 December 2016 for the concessional and transfer balance caps, 31 December 2025 for the Division 296 thresholds)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the super cap indexation factor` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`index number for the December quarter before the year` DIVIDED BY `index number for the base quarter`) TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5)
        DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 960-285(2): "You index the amount by: (a) first, multiplying its base amount mentioned in subsection (3) by its *indexation
-- factor mentioned in subsection (5); and (b) next, rounding the result in paragraph (a) down to the nearest multiple of its
-- *rounding amount." (4): "You do not index the amount if the *indexation factor is 1 or less." -- the base amount stands.
GIVEN `base amount` IS A NUMBER
      `rounding amount` IS A NUMBER
      `factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount indexed under s 960-285` MEANS
    IF `factor` AT MOST 1 THEN `base amount`
    ELSE FLOOR (`base amount` TIMES `factor` DIVIDED BY `rounding amount`) TIMES `rounding amount`

-- s 960-285(3)(b) and (5)(b): items 9 and 10A (the concessional cap and the general transfer balance cap) index "the amount for
-- the 2017-2018 financial year" from "the quarter ending on 31 December 2016"; (3)(c) and (5)(c): items 10B and 10C (the
-- Division 296 thresholds) index "the amount for the 2026-27 income year" from "the quarter ending on 31 December 2025".
-- (7) table: item 2 (concessional cap) -- AWOTE, rounding amount $2,500; item 3 (general transfer balance cap) -- CPI, $100,000;
-- item 4 (large superannuation balance threshold) -- CPI, $150,000; item 5 (very large) -- CPI, $500,000.
-- Before the base year the provision gives no amount: NOTHING.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
      `base year` IS A NUMBER
      `base amount` IS A NUMBER
      `rounding amount` IS A NUMBER
      `index number for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER
      `index number for the base quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the cap for the year` MEANS
    IF `year` LESS THAN `base year` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `year` EQUALS `base year` THEN JUST `base amount`
         ELSE JUST (`the amount indexed under s 960-285` `base amount` `rounding amount`
                       (`What is the super cap indexation factor` `index number for the December quarter before the year` `index number for the base quarter`))

-- s 291-20(2): "(a) for the 2017-2018 financial year -- $25,000; or (b) for the 2018-2019 financial year or a later financial
-- year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually the amount mentioned in paragraph (a)."
@export What is the concessional contributions cap for a financial year (ss 291-20(2), 960-285)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins (2025 for 2025-26)
      `AWOTE index for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings for November of the year before (the middle month of the December quarter), as first published
      `AWOTE index for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The same AWOTE estimate for November 2016
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the concessional contributions cap` MEANS
    `the cap for the year` `year` 2017 25000 2500 `AWOTE index for the December quarter before the year` `AWOTE index for the December 2016 quarter`

-- s 294-35(3): "(a) for the 2017-2018 *financial year -- $1,600,000; or (b) for the 2018-2019 financial year or a later financial
-- year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually the amount mentioned in paragraph (a)."
@export What is the general transfer balance cap for a financial year (ss 294-35(3), 960-285)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins
      `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number (8 capitals) first published for the quarter ending 31 December just before the year
      `CPI for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter ending 31 December 2016
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the general transfer balance cap` MEANS
    `the cap for the year` `year` 2017 1600000 100000 `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2016 quarter`

-- s 296-30: "(a) for the 2026-27 income year -- $3,000,000; or (b) for the 2027-28 income year or a later income year -- the
-- amount worked out by indexing annually the amount mentioned in paragraph (a)." s 296-35: the same with $10,000,000.
@export What is the large superannuation balance threshold for an income year (ss 296-30, 960-285)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year begins (2026 for 2026-27)
      `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter ending 31 December just before the year
      `CPI for the December 2025 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter ending 31 December 2025
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the large superannuation balance threshold` MEANS
    `the cap for the year` `year` 2026 3000000 150000 `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2025 quarter`

@export What is the very large superannuation balance threshold for an income year (ss 296-35, 960-285)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year begins (2026 for 2026-27)
      `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter ending 31 December just before the year
      `CPI for the December 2025 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter ending 31 December 2025
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the very large superannuation balance threshold` MEANS
    `the cap for the year` `year` 2026 10000000 500000 `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2025 quarter`

§§ `292-85(2) -- the non-concessional cap, from the index numbers`

-- itaa-super.l4's `What is my non-concessional cap` (s 292-85(2)) with both caps worked out above rather than supplied.
@export What is my non-concessional contributions cap, worked out from the published index numbers (ss 292-85(2), 291-20(2), 294-35(3))?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins
      `AWOTE index for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc AWOTE (full-time adult, ordinary time) for November of the year before, as first published
      `AWOTE index for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc AWOTE for November 2016, as first published
      `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number for the quarter ending 31 December just before the year
      `CPI for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number for the quarter ending 31 December 2016
      `total superannuation balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation balance just before the start of the year, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my non-concessional cap from the index numbers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is the concessional contributions cap` `year` `AWOTE index for the December quarter before the year` `AWOTE index for the December 2016 quarter`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `concessional` THEN
        CONSIDER `What is the general transfer balance cap` `year` `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2016 quarter`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `general` THEN JUST (`What is my non-concessional cap` `concessional` `total superannuation balance` `general`)

§§ `294-40 -- proportional indexation of my transfer balance cap`

-- s 294-40(1): applies to increase your cap for a later financial year if "(a) the *general transfer balance cap is increased as
-- a result of indexation for the financial year; and (b) at no time before the start of that financial year has the *transfer
-- balance in your transfer balance account at the end of a day exceeded your transfer balance cap."
-- (2), from the authorised rendering:   Unused cap percentage × Indexation increase
-- "indexation increase means the amount by which the *general transfer balance cap for the *financial year increased as a result
-- of indexation." "unused cap percentage is worked out by: (a) identifying the highest *transfer balance ... at the end of any day
-- up to the end of the previous *financial year; (b) identifying the day ... (the earliest of those days); (c) expressing the
-- transfer balance identified in paragraph (a) as a percentage (rounded down to the nearest whole number) of your *transfer
-- balance cap on the day identified in paragraph (b); and (d) subtracting the result of paragraph (c) from 100%."
-- (3): "if the highest *transfer balance ... is less than nil, that unused cap percentage is taken to be 100%."
@export What is my unused cap percentage, in percent (s 294-40(2), (3))?
GIVEN `highest transfer balance so far` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest transfer balance at the end of any day up to the end of the previous financial year, in dollars
      `my cap on the day of that balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your transfer balance cap on the (earliest) day your account had that balance, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my unused cap percentage` MEANS
    IF `highest transfer balance so far` LESS THAN 0 THEN 100
    ELSE 100 MINUS FLOOR (`highest transfer balance so far` DIVIDED BY `my cap on the day of that balance` TIMES 100)

-- s 294-35(2): "Your transfer balance cap for a later *financial year is equal to your transfer balance cap for the previous year,
-- subject to section 294-40". The answer cannot go below the previous year's cap: a negative unused percentage (a balance once
-- above the cap) is excluded by (1)(b), so it gives no increase.
@export What is my transfer balance cap for a later financial year (ss 294-35(2), 294-40)?
GIVEN `my cap for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own transfer balance cap for the previous financial year, in dollars
      `general cap for this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for this financial year, in dollars
      `general cap for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for the previous financial year, in dollars
      `ever exceeded my cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the end of any day before this financial year, your transfer balance exceeded your cap
      `highest transfer balance so far` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest transfer balance at the end of any day up to the end of the previous financial year, in dollars
      `my cap on the day of that balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your transfer balance cap on the (earliest) day your account had that balance, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my transfer balance cap for a later year` MEANS
    IF `general cap for this year` GREATER THAN `general cap for the previous year` AND (NOT `ever exceeded my cap`)
    THEN `my cap for the previous year` PLUS `the increase`
    ELSE `my cap for the previous year`
    WHERE
        `the unused percentage` MEANS `What is my unused cap percentage` `highest transfer balance so far` `my cap on the day of that balance`
        `the indexation increase` MEANS `general cap for this year` MINUS `general cap for the previous year`
        `the increase` MEANS (`the unused percentage` TIMES `the indexation increase`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- itaa-super.l4's `What is my excess transfer balance` (s 294-30) on a cap worked out under s 294-40.
@export Do I have an excess transfer balance in a later year, with my cap proportionally indexed (ss 294-30, 294-40)?
GIVEN `credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Transfer balance credits in your account, in dollars
      `debits` IS A NUMBER @desc Transfer balance debits in your account, in dollars
      `my cap for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your own transfer balance cap for the previous financial year, in dollars
      `general cap for this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for this financial year, in dollars
      `general cap for the previous year` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for the previous financial year, in dollars
      `ever exceeded my cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the end of any day before this financial year, your transfer balance exceeded your cap
      `highest transfer balance so far` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest transfer balance at the end of any day up to the end of the previous financial year, in dollars
      `my cap on the day of that balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your transfer balance cap on the (earliest) day your account had that balance, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my excess transfer balance in a later year` MEANS
    `What is my excess transfer balance` `credits` `debits`
        (`What is my transfer balance cap for a later year` `my cap for the previous year` `general cap for this year` `general cap for the previous year`
            `ever exceeded my cap` `highest transfer balance so far` `my cap on the day of that balance`)

§§ `303-4(1) -- defined benefit income cap`

-- s 303-4(1), from the authorised rendering: "Your defined benefit income cap for a *financial year is the following amount
-- (rounded up to the nearest dollar):   The *general transfer balance cap for the *financial year / 16"
@export What is my defined benefit income cap for a full financial year (s 303-4(1))?
GIVEN `general transfer balance cap` IS A NUMBER @desc The general transfer balance cap for the financial year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my defined benefit income cap` MEANS
    CEILING (`general transfer balance cap` DIVIDED BY 16)

§§ `296-40, 296-45 -- Division 296: the part of my super earnings that is taxed`

-- s 296-40(1): "You have taxable superannuation earnings for an income year of the amount worked out using the following formula
-- if: (a) your *total superannuation balance just before the start of the year, or at the end of the year, is greater than the
-- *large superannuation balance threshold for the year; and (b) the amount of your *total superannuation earnings for the year is
-- greater than nil:" -- from the authorised rendering:
--     The percentage worked out under subsections (2) and (3) × The amount of your *total superannuation earnings for the year
-- (2): ((Your total superannuation balance reference amount − The *large superannuation balance threshold for the year) / Your
-- total superannuation balance reference amount) × 100; "your total superannuation balance reference amount is the greater of:
-- (a) your *total superannuation balance (if any) just before the start of the year; and (b) ... at the end of the year."
-- (3): "rounded to 2 decimal places (rounding up if the third decimal place is 5 or more)."
-- s 296-45: the same with the *very large superannuation balance threshold, for the very large superannuation balance earnings
-- component; its condition (s 296-45(1)) is the balance alone, without (1)(b)'s "greater than nil" for the earnings, and the
-- encoding keeps that difference. ss 296-20, 296-25 (a child recipient of an income stream; a structured settlement contribution): one fact.
GIVEN `balance just before the start of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `balance at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Division 296 percentage` MEANS
    FLOOR (((`the reference amount` MINUS `threshold`) DIVIDED BY `the reference amount`) TIMES 100 TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the reference amount` MEANS `the larger amount of` `balance just before the start of the year` `balance at the end of the year`

GIVEN `balance just before the start of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `balance at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `total superannuation earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Division 296 amount` MEANS
    IF     (`balance just before the start of the year` GREATER THAN `threshold` OR `balance at the end of the year` GREATER THAN `threshold`)
       AND `total superannuation earnings` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the earnings at the Division 296 percentage` `balance just before the start of the year` `balance at the end of the year` `threshold` `total superannuation earnings`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `balance just before the start of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `balance at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `total superannuation earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings at the Division 296 percentage` MEANS
    (`the percentage` TIMES `total superannuation earnings`) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the percentage` MEANS `the Division 296 percentage` `balance just before the start of the year` `balance at the end of the year` `threshold`

@export What are my taxable superannuation earnings for the income year (ss 296-15 to 296-40)?
GIVEN `an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child recipient of a super income stream in the year, or a structured settlement contribution has ever been made for you (ss 296-20, 296-25)
      `balance just before the start of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation balance just before the start of the income year, in dollars
      `balance at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation balance at the end of the income year, in dollars
      `large superannuation balance threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The large superannuation balance threshold for the year ($3,000,000 for 2026-27, indexed after)
      `total superannuation earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation earnings for the year under s 296-55, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my taxable superannuation earnings` MEANS
    IF `an exception applies` THEN 0
    ELSE `the Division 296 amount` `balance just before the start of the year` `balance at the end of the year` `large superannuation balance threshold` `total superannuation earnings`

@export What is my very large superannuation balance earnings component for the income year (s 296-45)?
GIVEN `balance just before the start of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation balance just before the start of the income year, in dollars
      `balance at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation balance at the end of the income year, in dollars
      `very large superannuation balance threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The very large superannuation balance threshold for the year ($10,000,000 for 2026-27, indexed after)
      `total superannuation earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total superannuation earnings for the year under s 296-55, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my very large balance earnings component` MEANS
    IF `balance just before the start of the year` GREATER THAN `very large superannuation balance threshold` OR `balance at the end of the year` GREATER THAN `very large superannuation balance threshold`
    THEN `the earnings at the Division 296 percentage` `balance just before the start of the year` `balance at the end of the year` `very large superannuation balance threshold` `total superannuation earnings`
    ELSE 0
